$ grep -n "Allowed bots are not checked" security.md
7:  - **⚠️ Allowed bots are not checked for repository permissions.** A bot that matches an entry does **not** need to be installed on your repository or have write access. On a **public repository**, external parties — including GitHub Apps created by anyone — may be able to trigger workflow events such as opening issues, commenting, or reviewing pull requests. If your workflow listens on those events and `allowed_bots` is set to `'*'`, any such App can invoke this action with a prompt it controls.

